    {
      "title": "It's easy to love Atom, a likeable underdog movie review",
      "snippet": "My complaint about the battling Transformers of the movies series is that they resemble incomprehensible piles of auto parts thrown at each other. Fast cutting is used to disguise the lack of spatial continuity. \"Real Steel,\" however, slows down the fight action enough so that we can actually perceive it, and the boxing makes sense.",
      "link": "www.rogerebert.com/reviews/real-steel-2011"
    },
